>769</fpage><lpage>773</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2271377</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003461-Karson1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karson</surname><given-names>CN</given-names></name></person-group><year>1983</year><article-title>Spontaneous eye-blink rates and dopaminergic systems.</article-title><source>Brain</source><volume>106</volume><fpage>643</fpage><lpage>653</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6640274</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003461-Kleven1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kleven</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Koek</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Differential effects of direct and indirect dopamine agonists on eye blink rate in cynomolgus monkeys.</article-title><source>J Pharmacol Exp Ther</source><volume>279</volume><fpage>1211</fpage><lpage>1219</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8968343</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003461-Taylor1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Elsworth</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Lawrence</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Sladek</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Roth</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Spontaneous blink rates correlate with dopamine levels in the caudate nucleus of MPTP-treated monkeys.</article-title><source>Exp Neurol</source><volume>158</volume><fpage>214</fpage><lpage>220</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10448434</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003461-Freed1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="au